course: dictionary
lesson: 13607
title: Incumbent: the one in the job now
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An incumbent is the person who holds a job right now, especially an important official job. Read the words around it for clues. «The incumbent mayor wants to win the election again.» The clue is that the mayor already has the job, so the incumbent is the person who already has it.
explain: Look for the opposite person. «The challenger wants to take the job from the incumbent.» The challenger is the one who wants the job but does not have it yet. The incumbent is the one who already has it. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The person who already holds the job wants to win the election again» still makes sense.
explain: Incumbent has a second meaning about duty. «It is incumbent on you to tell the truth.» Here it means it is your duty, so you must do it. Try swapping in «your duty»: «It is your duty to tell the truth» works, so you have the right meaning.
fact: An incumbent is the person who holds an official job right now, such as a mayor, president or member of parliament.
fact: A challenger is the person who wants to take the job from the incumbent.
fact: «Incumbent on» or «incumbent upon» someone means it is their duty, so they must do it.
fact: In a church, the incumbent of a parish is the priest or vicar in charge of it.
fact: A quick check: if someone already has the job, they are the incumbent; if they want it, they are the challenger.
exercise: «The incumbent won the election again.» Who is the incumbent? | The person who wants to win the job | *The person who already holds the job | A paper slip used for voting | The room where people vote
exercise: «It is incumbent on you to wash your hands before lunch.» What does incumbent on you mean here? | It is a kind of lunch | It is your favourite game | *It is your duty | You are allowed to skip it
exercise: «The challenger hopes to defeat the incumbent mayor.» Who is the incumbent mayor? | The challenger who wants the job | The reporter writing the news | The voters on the day of the election | *The mayor who already holds the job
test: «Our vicar is the incumbent of this parish.» In a church, what is an incumbent? | *The priest or vicar in charge of the parish | A visitor who comes to sing | The leader of the church choir | The person who rings the bell
test: Lily says, «It is incumbent upon all of us to look after the park.» What does incumbent upon us mean? | We might do it one day | *It is our duty | It is a game we like | We are too tired to help
exam: Ben reads, «The incumbent holds the job now, but the challenger wants it.» Which word means the person who wants a job they do not have yet? | Parish | Duty | Incumbent | *Challenger
